2. General permission

Subject to Sections 3 through 7 and preservation of applicable notices, you
may play, run, study, copy, modify, and share the covered material. Ordinary
play, private internal use, and private classroom use remain permitted
regardless of revenue, except that the separate AI-training condition in
Section 5 still applies to qualifying training activities. This license
grants no rights over third-party material beyond its own terms.

3. Company and revenue threshold

For Sections 4 and 5, a Company means a business or other legal entity,
including a for-profit or nonprofit corporation, partnership, or educational
institution. There is no automatic educational-institution exemption.

A Company is above the threshold when its gross annual revenue, including
that of its controlled subsidiaries, exceeds US$1,000,000 for the most
recently completed fiscal year. The threshold is strictly over US$1,000,000,
not equal to that amount, and concerns total entity-wide revenue rather than
revenue from this game, hosting service, dataset, or model. Convert revenue
to US dollars using that year's average exchange rate from an identified
recognized public financial source.

The separate written permissions in Sections 4 and 5 are independent. A
Company need not both host and train to trigger either applicable condition.
A contractor or intermediary performing a restricted activity on behalf of
an above-threshold Company requires the written permission applicable to
that activity; using an intermediary does not remove the condition.

4. Public game hosting

A Company above the threshold must obtain a separate written commercial
hosting license from Titans Forge LLC before hosting covered material or a
modified version of it. Hosting means making a playable copy or interactive
game instance publicly available to others through a website, application,
or game service. The condition applies whether or not players are charged.
Companies at or below the threshold do not require separate hosting
permission under this section.

Ordinary play, private internal/classroom play, a link to an official game
page, and an embedded player whose game is actually served by an authorized
distribution platform are not hosting one's own copy. Hosting elsewhere
still requires the rights applicable to that copy; an iframe or proxy does
not waive those rights. These terms preserve itch.io's existing platform
distribution authorization and any other separately granted distribution
permission. Forge may separately authorize an Apple or other platform
edition without changing the terms of other editions. Permission to host
or distribute does not by itself grant permission for AI training.

5. AI training and training datasets

A Company above the threshold must obtain a separate written AI-training
license from Titans Forge LLC before using covered material to train,
fine-tune, or distill an artificial-intelligence or machine-learning model,
or to create or distribute a dataset intended for those activities by or on
behalf of an above-threshold Company. This includes using covered code,
text, artwork, audio, or other protected expression as training examples,
where that use requires permission from the Licensor.

This condition applies independently of public hosting, model publication,
charging a fee, and the commercial or research purpose of the model. It
also applies to qualifying private, internal, and classroom training;
the general private/classroom-use permission is not a training exemption.
Companies at or below the threshold do not require separate AI-training
permission under this section unless acting on behalf of an
above-threshold Company as described in Section 3.

Merely playing or modifying the game, ordinary search indexing, inference,
and using an existing AI tool to explain, test, or help edit the material
without training, fine-tuning, or distilling a model on it do not trigger
this section. An ordinary retrieval index, including an embedding index
created with unchanged model weights, is not model training under these
terms. These exceptions do not grant a tool provider separate permission
to train on covered material. Nothing here claims control over historical
facts, public-domain material, independently licensed material, or uses
permitted independently by applicable law.

